0.00.837.163 I report_host_expert_placement: the host-expert tier is PINNED BY NECESSITY whatever --load-mode says: an RDNA GPU has no XNACK, so a device read of a host-resident expert must come from a page the kernel has already made resident (the bounded pinned pool in front of the pageable hole set), and every device read of the tier is served from it.  `--load-mode mlock`/`mmap+mlock` therefore adds nothing for the host experts -- the pin it buys belongs to the tensors the CPU reads (a CPU-only or partly CPU-offloaded run) and to the load itself.
